The client entrypoint belongs in **`StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts`**, but right now it won't run.

`default.project.json` maps `src/client` to `ReplicatedStorage.Client`. Rojo turns `init.client.luau` into a LocalScript there, and LocalScripts in ReplicatedStorage never run. The `print("client")` in `src/client/init.client.luau` would never execute. The server side is fine: `src/server` maps to `ServerScriptService.Server`, which is a place where Scripts run.

The fix is to change the mapping in `default.project.json`:

```json
{
  "name": "arena",
  "tree": {
    "$className": "DataModel",
    "ReplicatedStorage": {
      "Shared": { "$path": "src/shared" },
      "Packages": { "$path": "Packages" }
    },
    "ServerScriptService": { "Server": { "$path": "src/server" } },
    "StarterPlayer": {
      "StarterPlayerScripts": {
        "Client": { "$path": "src/client" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Client code can still `require` shared modules from `ReplicatedStorage.Shared`, so nothing else needs to move. The files in `src/client` stay where they are. They just become children of the client LocalScript instead of living in ReplicatedStorage.

